# What is uploaded when CI runs `vercel deploy --prod` from source.
#
# This file exists to make that answer deterministic. Without it the CLI falls
# back to `.gitignore`, and `.gitignore` excludes `public/build-health.json` —
# the one file CI writes immediately before deploying and the one the staged and
# public smokes read to decide whether the release is the commit it claims to
# be. The deploy would have uploaded everything except its own evidence, and the
# smoke would have failed on a file that was never sent rather than on anything
# wrong with the release.
#
# So: an explicit list, and `public/build-health.json` is deliberately not on it.
# Everything here is either rebuilt on Vercel, local-only state, or something
# that must never leave this machine.

# Rebuilt on Vercel
node_modules
.next
out
build

# Local state and tooling
.git
.vercel
.claude
.claude-flow
.swarm
.hive-mind
supabase/.branches
supabase/.temp

# Verification artefacts
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.playwright
.lighthouseci

# Recovery material — encrypted archives, keys and plaintext dumps
.backups
.db-gate
*.agekey
*.dump
*.dump.age
*.tar.gz.age

# Secrets and machine files
.env*
*.pem
.DS_Store
._*
*.tsbuildinfo
